# Cursor Agent Operating Rules (Project-Level)

This project requires strict spec-first and rule-first execution for every AI coding task.

## Mandatory Priority Order

When there is any ambiguity or conflict, apply this order:

1. `docs/specs/001-housemaid-booking-api/spec.md` and related files in `docs/specs/**`
2. `.cursor/rules/spec-alignment.mdc`
3. Other project rules in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`
4. Project skills in `.agents/skills/**/SKILL.md`
5. Generic/global skills only when not conflicting with project rules

## Always-Apply Requirements For Every Coding Task

- Read relevant `docs/specs/**` documents before implementing API or business logic.
- Keep endpoint behavior aligned with locked requirements (`FR-043` to `FR-047`) when applicable.
- Follow project architecture: `controller -> service -> repository`.
- Keep handlers thin in `app/controllers/`; business logic in `app/services/`; data access in repositories.
- Use project response/error conventions (`ResponseBuilder`, structured errors).
- Enforce strict RBAC and role boundaries (customer/helper/staff/admin).
- Add or update tests for happy path and important error paths.
- Run quality checks before finishing (`poetry run pre-commit run --all-files`) when code changes are made.

## Skills and Rules Enforcement

- Always apply project rules under `.cursor/rules/`.
- Prefer project skills under `.agents/skills/` before using generic templates.
- When the user asks to create a commit (or mentions `/commit`), prioritize the project skill `.agents/skills/git-commit/SKILL.md`.
- For commit tasks, keep workflow safe and non-interactive: avoid `git add -p`, never use destructive git commands, never skip hooks unless explicitly requested.
- Do not introduce code patterns that conflict with project rules or specs.
- If a generic skill conflicts with this repository rules/specs, ignore the generic guidance.

## API-Specific Guardrails

- Booking creation requires quote-first flow (`quote_id`) per FR-043.
- Helper KYC upload must follow presigned-upload constraints per FR-044.
- Internal staff/admin auth must follow single-issuer JWT behavior per FR-045.
- Public APIs must implement consistent rate limit behavior and structured `429` per FR-046.
- Return `403` for eligibility failure and `422` for invalid payload semantics per FR-047.

## Delivery Behavior

- If requested task is implementation, perform end-to-end changes instead of giving only plans.
- Keep scope aligned with the role/module under `docs/specs/{customer,helper,admin}/`.
- Do not silently bypass specs; raise a clear note if any requested change conflicts with specs.
